{"game": "mass-effect-andromeda", "language": "english", "appid": 1238000, "month": "2026-08", "window": 4, "start_date": 1787529600, "end_date": 1788220799, "month_true_total": 116, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-07 22:03:41 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "234153135", "author": {"steamid": "76561198038561954", "personaname": "EternalNoob", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198038561954/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 38, "playtime_forever": 1316, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1111, "last_played": 1790057655, "avatar": "5e678ff759bb4d5bd92b9e45f598f31fb068cf5d"}, "language": "english", "review": "Gave it a fair shot, 16 hours & three planets cleared, but I'm done.\r\n\r\nAndromeda has the Mass Effect name, races and some aesthetics, but it doesn't feel like Mass Effect at all.\r\nThe tight mission > ship > crew > story structure has been replaced by a sprawling RPG full of side quests, scanning, monoliths, mining, vaults and viability meters.\r\n\r\nThe Tempest and companions are decent, but they're buried under too much busywork. \r\nThe Angara look like someone started designing a cute alien with big floppy ears and gave up mid way, the main villain looks permanently cross because someone took his pacifier away.\r\nThe repetitive Remnant vaults finally killed it for me.\r\n\r\nMaybe a decent sci-fi RPG, but not the Mass Effect experience I was looking for.", "timestamp_created": 1788173855, "timestamp_updated": 1788173855, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887420", "hardware": {"system_ram": "32362", "os": "Windows 11", "cpu_name": "AMD Ryzen 5 7500F 6-Core Processor             ", "adapter_description": "NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060", 